module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster_is_its_own_denominator

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data roster_is_its_own_denominator: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "roster_is_its_own_denominator" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a roster is its own denominator, so the instrument reading it cannot notice the roster is short** (INVALID STATE: a report enumerates the rows a hand-authored roster happens to hold, renders a verdict per row, and presents the result as an answer ABOUT THE SUBJECT -- while no independent authority states how many identities that subject should have, so a subject missing rows renders as a complete block and reads as a complete answer. ",

    "HARM: every way a roster can lose a row -- a partial edit, a bad merge, a branch mix-up, a deletion nobody reviewed, a row never added -- produces a receipt indistinguishable from the whole truth. The receipt is not wrong about the rows it names; it is silent about the ones it was never asked. And because the silence is total, the reader's only defence is to already know the answer, which is exactly what they consulted the instrument to learn. ",

    "THE SPECIMEN, found by execution and by an author's own mistake rather than by review (2026-09-04, import-cut lane): gunbc.namespace_cut_subject_observation subject_roster_report was run to establish that the namespace cut's probe identities are PRESENT before the cut. It rendered the ResolverImportNameUniverse subject as three PRESENT rows and stopped. Three further probes belonging to that same subject existed on a different branch and were absent from the tree that ran. The block was well-formed, fully green, and short by half, and nothing in the output distinguished it from the complete subject. The defect was caught only because the author independently remembered that three more probes should be there. ",

    "WHY IT IS NOT ONE OF THE ROWS BESIDE IT, checked rather than assumed, because three neighbours are close enough to be tempting. ",

    "It is not `selection_view_read_as_population`: that class turns on membership computed from a MEASURED quantity, so the set moves when the instrument or the load moves. Nothing here is measured -- the roster is hand-authored and perfectly stable -- and the set moves only when an author edits it. The defect is that the authored set is UNJOINED to any statement of what it should be, not that a threshold slid. ",

    "It is not `check_subject_narrower_than_its_declared_claim`: there, an implementation ranges over less than the claim it is cited for, and the claim exists to be compared against. Here there is NO independent claim about cardinality at all -- the roster is simultaneously the subject definition and the evidence of its own completeness, which is why the comparison that would expose the gap has nothing to stand on. That class is a gap between two statements; this one is the absence of the second statement. ",

    "It is not `green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own`: that instrument denominates a real population correctly and merely does not own all of it. This instrument denominates NOTHING -- it has no population, only a list. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: outside the ladder, and this is the honest placement rather than a low one. The gap is invisible from the instrument's own result for the same reason a wall over a clean corpus is green, so there is no executed evidence that could currently discriminate a complete subject from a short one. Naming it mitigatable would be inflation, because nothing contains the harm: the receipt is consumed as though it were total. ",

    "CEILING: structurally guaranteed. Whether a subject's probe set is complete is decidable ONCE an independent authority states the expected identities, and that authority is derivable rather than hand-countable -- which is what keeps this off the ratchet-forever arm and out of a numeric-literal oracle. A literal expected-count per subject would be the count equality DESIGN section 5 forbids: completeness is an identity join. ",

    "TRIGGER, FIRST FORM, AND WHY IT WAS UNDER-SPECIFIED -- recorded rather than silently replaced, because the correction is the instructive part. The row first named the trigger as: an independently derived statement of each subject's expected identities, joined at identity grain, refusing a subject the roster does not cover. That is a real climb and it is NOT the structural one. Two lists plus an exact set-equality gate reaches MECHANICALLY PREVENTABLE and stops there, because BOTH lists stay writable and an omission is still an edit the two can share -- a single author dropping a subject from the expected list and the roster in one change satisfies the gate perfectly. Naming a second authority as the trigger for a STRUCTURAL ceiling was the artifact-shaped trigger this ledger warns about, committed inside the row that exists to warn about denominators. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMING THE CAPABILITY: the operational roster is DERIVED as a TOTAL PROJECTION from a closed expected-root coproduct -- so every expected root has a constructor, the projection is exhaustive over it, and a subject omitted from the roster has no way to be written rather than merely being caught. At that point the roster cannot disagree with its denominator because it is not a second list; it is the denominator viewed through a total function. The set-equality gate remains legitimate as the RUNG-2 step on the way there, and it must not be reported as the ceiling reached. ",

    "WHY IT IS URGENT RATHER THAN INTERESTING: this instrument sits inside the exit criterion of the namespace cut. The final head is to be accepted on its testimony that both import authorities are ABSENT -- and absence is precisely the verdict this defect cannot distinguish from not-having-been-asked. A short roster at the final head would report the cut complete. The class must climb before that receipt is cited, not after. ",

    "SECOND SPECIMEN, AND IT SHOWS THE CLASS DOES NOT NEED A MISSING ROW -- A ROW THAT STOPPED NAMING ANYTHING IS ENOUGH. v2.test.claim.complexity.accumulator_copy_roster_gate enumerates nine paths for the copied-accumulator lens to analyse. One of them, src/v2/workflow/glob_discovery_law.dag, moved to src/v2/test/workflow/ in the #9637 directory reorganisation and the roster row was not repointed. The roster is its own denominator here in the sharpest way available: nothing states which of the corpus the nine are supposed to stand for, so a row that decayed into naming nothing is indistinguishable from a row that is doing its job, and the gate being operator-ruled OFFLINE meant no consumer executed it to find out. ",

    "AND THE FAILURE ARM MADE IT WORSE THAN SILENT -- IT WAS ABSORBING. The subject read went through the filesystem_read intrinsic, whose result type carries content and no success channel, so the missing path raised an interpreter type error and ended the process. At roster grain that reads as one red test; at corpus grain every subject after the missing one is never asked, which is the same silence this row describes arriving through a loud door. Repaired by folding the read through extdeps.filesystem.filesystem_io filesystem_read_outcome and giving the analysis-standing coproduct a SourceUnreadable arm, so an unreadable subject is one typed counted row and the sweep continues; the discriminating control is v2.test.claim.complexity.accumulator_copy_unreadable_subject, which on the pre-fix build fails with a runtime error rather than a false. ",

    "WHAT THE REPAIR DOES NOT DO, stated so the specimen is not read as a climb it did not earn. Repointing a stale row and typing the read leave the roster a hand-authored list with no denominator. The population question is answered separately by v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.corpus_gate, whose subjects come from the module index rather than from an author -- the derivation the trigger above asks for, at the one grain where a total projection was already available. It does not retire the trigger: the corpus consumer is priced out of every cadence by interpreted ingest, so the roster is still what executes. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE: when a report's rows come from a hand-authored list, ask what would happen if a row were deleted -- if the answer is 'the report renders one fewer row and says nothing', the list is acting as its own denominator and the report's completeness is an unstated assumption rather than a checked fact.)",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
